---
<PolicyLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="The rules that keep BeeGreat useful, fair, and safe for everyone using Bee and the BeeGreat services."
  eyebrow="BeeGreat legal"
  updated="July 16, 2026"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section aria-labelledby="agreement">
    <h2 id="agreement">Agreement and eligibility</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms of Use (“Terms”) form an agreement between you and BeeGreat (“BeeGreat,” “we,” “us,” or “our”) and govern your use of the BeeGreat mobile app, BeeDocs website, Bee assistant, and related services (together, the “Service”). By downloading, accessing, or using the Service—or purchasing BeeGreat Pro—you agree to these Terms and our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you do not agree, do not use the Service. You must be at least 13 years old and legally able to enter into this agreement. If local law requires a higher minimum age, that higher age applies. If you use BeeGreat for an organization, you represent that you have authority to bind it to these Terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="service">
    <h2 id="service">The BeeGreat service</h2>
    <p>
      BeeGreat is a personal focus and productivity service. It can help you plan goals, projects, and tasks; keep conversations and memories you choose to save; use voice or text with Bee; track progress in your Hive; and enable optional connections or power-ups.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Service evolves. We may add, change, suspend, or discontinue features to improve reliability, safety, legal compliance, or the product itself. We will provide reasonable notice when a material change negatively affects a paid feature, unless urgent security, legal, or technical circumstances make advance notice impractical.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="subscription">
    <h2 id="subscription">BeeGreat Pro subscription</h2>
    <p>
      BeeGreat Pro is a monthly auto-renewing subscription that unlocks the paid BeeGreat experience. The United States App Store price is <strong>US$6.99 per month</strong>. Taxes and prices in other currencies or regions may differ. The price and billing terms shown in Apple’s purchase sheet when you confirm the transaction control your purchase.
    </p>
    <div class="policy-note">
      <p><strong>Auto-renewal:</strong> payment is charged to your Apple Account when you confirm the purchase. Your subscription renews automatically each month unless you turn off auto-renewal at least 24 hours before the current billing period ends. Apple may charge your account for renewal within 24 hours before that period ends.</p>
    </div>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Manage or cancel.</strong> Manage your subscription in your device’s Settings under your Apple Account and Subscriptions, or visit <a href="https://apps.apple.com/account/subscriptions">Apple’s subscription page</a>. Cancellation stops future renewals; access ordinarily continues through the end of the paid period.</li>
      <li><strong>Restore.</strong> Use “Restore Purchases” in BeeGreat when you reinstall the app or move to another device. Restoration requires the Apple Account that made the purchase and the corresponding BeeGreat account.</li>
      <li><strong>Refunds.</strong> Apple processes App Store billing and refund requests under its policies. You can request help at <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com/">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Trials and offers.</strong> No free trial is included unless Apple’s purchase sheet explicitly displays one. Any offer-specific terms shown there apply.</li>
      <li><strong>Price changes.</strong> Apple will provide any notice or consent required for a subscription price increase. If you do not accept a change that requires consent, your subscription may not renew.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Deleting BeeGreat or your BeeGreat account does not automatically cancel an Apple subscription. Cancel through Apple separately if you do not want it to renew.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="accounts">
    <h2 id="accounts">Accounts and security</h2>
    <p>
      You need an account to use most of BeeGreat. Give us accurate information, keep your sign-in method and devices secure, and tell us promptly if you believe your account has been compromised. You are responsible for activity performed through your account unless it results from our failure to use reasonable security measures.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may not sell, transfer, or share an account in a way that bypasses subscription, security, or usage limits. We may require you to re-authenticate or reconnect a third-party service to protect your account.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="content">
    <h2 id="content">Your content</h2>
    <p>
      You retain ownership of the prompts, messages, goals, tasks, files, memories, instructions, and other content you submit to BeeGreat (“Your Content”). You grant BeeGreat a limited, non-exclusive, worldwide license to host, copy, transmit, transform, and otherwise process Your Content only as reasonably necessary to provide, secure, troubleshoot, and support the Service and to comply with law.
    </p>
    <p>
      You represent that you have the rights needed to submit Your Content and that our processing of it as described in these Terms will not violate another person’s rights. You are responsible for reviewing content before you rely on, share, publish, or act on it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="acceptable-use">
    <h2 id="acceptable-use">Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>You may not use the Service to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>break the law, infringe intellectual-property or privacy rights, or facilitate fraud, harassment, abuse, or exploitation;</li>
      <li>upload malware, probe or disrupt systems, defeat access controls, scrape at unreasonable scale, or interfere with another person’s use;</li>
      <li>misrepresent AI-generated material as verified fact where that could cause harm;</li>
      <li>obtain unauthorized access to accounts, connected services, health information, wallets, or credentials;</li>
      <li>reverse engineer or extract protected parts of the Service except where applicable law expressly permits it; or</li>
      <li>resell, sublicense, or use the Service to build a competing model or service without our written permission.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We may apply reasonable technical and usage limits to protect the Service and manage provider costs.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="ai-health-web3">
    <h2 id="ai-health-web3">AI, health, and Web3</h2>
    <h3>AI output</h3>
    <p>
      Bee uses artificial intelligence. AI output may be incomplete, outdated, offensive, or wrong, and similar inputs can produce different results. Verify important information and use your own judgment. BeeGreat is not a substitute for a qualified professional and is not designed for emergency use.
    </p>

    <h3>Health information</h3>
    <p>
      The optional Google Health power-up is read-only and can help summarize information you authorize. BeeGreat is not a medical device, health-care provider, or emergency service. It does not diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any condition. Do not delay professional care because of Bee output. Contact local emergency services if you may be experiencing an emergency.
    </p>

    <h3>Web3 activity</h3>
    <p>
      The optional Web3 power-up may display public blockchain information or help submit wallet actions you approve. Digital assets can be volatile; networks may charge fees; and confirmed transactions may be irreversible. BeeGreat does not provide financial, investment, tax, or legal advice and does not guarantee the availability, value, or recovery of digital assets. Review every address, network, amount, and action before confirming it.
    </p>

    <h3>Generated media</h3>
    <p>
      The optional Imagine power-up sends prompts and source-media links you provide to FAL. Generation is probabilistic, may fail or produce unexpected material, and may incur provider costs or limits. You are responsible for having the rights to source media and for reviewing generated output before publishing or relying on it. Do not use Imagine to infringe intellectual-property, publicity, or privacy rights.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="third-parties">
    <h2 id="third-parties">Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      BeeGreat relies on service providers and can connect, at your direction, to third-party services such as ChatGPT, Google Health, GitHub, Linear, Notion, FAL, or a wallet provider. Those services have their own terms and privacy practices. You authorize us to exchange the information needed to provide the connection or generation you request.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not control third-party availability, content, or account decisions. Disconnecting inside BeeGreat stops future BeeGreat access, but you may also need to revoke access or manage data directly with the third party. Your use of Apple services is also subject to Apple’s applicable terms, including the <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/">Apple Media Services Terms and Conditions</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="ownership">
